    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n17431" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αὐλικός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αὐλή</span>)
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>of the court,
				courtier-like,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατὰ τὴν φύσιν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plb.
					23.5.4
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αὐ. ἀγχίνοια</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					15.34.4
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αὐ. βίος,</span> opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ φιλόσοφος βίος,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Phld.
				<u>Ind.Sto.</u>
				13
			</span></i>: 
				Comp.
			, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐξ αὐλικωτέρων γονέων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Lib.</u>
					p.45
				</span></i>
			 O.: as Subst., <i>courtier,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				16.20.8
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.778b
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Demetr.</u>
				17
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αὐλικούς: κιθαρῳδούς,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Suid.
			</span></i>
		</div>
